# Generated code is formatted by its generator, not by us.
#
# src/client/ is emitted by @hey-api/openapi-ts (`npm run generate-client`) and
# committed to git; the `contract` CI job regenerates it and fails on any diff.
# Formatting it here would be undone by the very next regeneration, putting the
# format:check gate and the contract gate in permanent conflict. ESLint already
# exempts this directory for the same reason (see eslint.config.js `ignores`).
src/client/

# Build and tooling output. Not matched by the src/** globs in package.json,
# listed so that an ad-hoc `npx prettier .` in this directory behaves too.
dist/
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# npm-generated lockfiles, on the same rule as src/client/ above: generated
# output is formatted by its generator, not by us. They agree with Prettier
# today, but npm owns these files, and a future npm whose output Prettier
# disagreed with would turn every dependency bump red over a file no human
# reads. Matches frontend/package-lock.json and design-system/package-lock.json.
package-lock.json
